  "summary_text": "Kyle, Port Washington ran hot yesterday\u2014$2,902 total revenue on four groomers, delivering $581 per groomer against a 30-day baseline of $475. That's a 22% productivity lift. Core grooming jumped 140% week-over-week, add-on attachment climbed to 71%, and retail gained 56%. This is what peak performance looks like. The week is tracking +29% and October, while down 5% nominally, is only -7.2% after adjusting for calendar headwinds\u2014so the real miss is modest and manageable. You should be proud of Port Washington's team discipline.\n\nHicksville is outperforming expectation. MTD it's up 16% against the calendar-adjusted expectation of +5.9%, and yesterday's three groomers hit $523 per groomer (27% above baseline). Appointments are up 19% month-to-date. The one soft spot: add-on attach fell from 31% to 24% yesterday, suggesting some upsell slippage on an otherwise strong day\u2014worth a coaching moment with the team.\n\nGlen Cove is concerning. Yesterday's two groomers produced only $290 per groomer ($244 baseline), but more troubling: next seven days show zero groomer-days scheduled. This location is operationally dark. You need immediate clarity on staffing intent here\u2014whether this is a planned staffing wind-down, a scheduling gap, or a retention issue. A $139k lapse pool at Hicksville and $318k at Port Washington suggests real reactivation upside if you want to lean in.\n\nPort Washington today: 1 groomer, 15 bather hours; tomorrow 5 groomers, 15 bather hours; next 7 days 36 groomer-days and 83 bather hours across both locations."
